WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.069
-The president
is already ramping up

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.004
his re-election campaign
as the specter

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:06.806
of Robert Mueller's report
looms over him.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.675
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:10.276
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:13.746 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:13.746 --> 00:00:16.215
Trump's campaign team
is signaling to reporters

00:00:16.215 --> 00:00:18.318
that they want to build
a massive re-election machine

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:19.786
with tons of money
and resources.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:21.254
But as CNN reported this week,

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:23.522
Trump's campaign also keeps
insisting to reporters

00:00:23.522 --> 00:00:25.759
that Trump, himself,
is in charge.

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:27.560
-We're getting
a rare exclusive look

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.729
inside the Trump 2020
re-election campaign

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.997
that's been humming since
his inauguration day.

00:00:31.997 --> 00:00:33.699
We're hearing about the changes
that they've made

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:35.067
to better use technology,

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:37.536
and as CNN's chief political
correspondent Dana Bash

00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:40.273
now reports, how even
the president's campaign manager

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:42.876
admits that Trump is
the communications director,

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:44.944
the finance director,
campaign manager,

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:47.447
and master of the Trump train.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.815
-I mean, maybe
he has all those jobs

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:52.585
because no one else
wants those jobs.

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:55.989
After the last --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:58.324
Remember,
after the last election,

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.493
his campaign chairman,
deputy campaign chairman,

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.695
national security adviser,
foreign policy adviser,

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.797
informal outside advisers,
and personal lawyer

00:01:04.797 --> 00:01:06.833
all got indicted
or went to jail.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:09.034
It's really hard to make
"Ocean's Twelve"

00:01:09.034 --> 00:01:11.871
when Ocean's Eleven
is facing 15 to 20.

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.339
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:16.142
If you get to job working for
Trump's re-election campaign,

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:19.078
they hand you an HR manual
and a jump suit.

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:21.447
I'm just kidding,
they don't have HR manuals.

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:22.848
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.848 --> 00:01:26.152
Also can we hear the list of
jobs Trump supposedly has again?

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:29.155
-Trump is the communications
director, the finance director,

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:32.892
campaign manager,
and master of the Trump train.

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:35.261
-Master of the Trump train
sounds like a fun one

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:38.164
they made up to keep his
attention in a meeting.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:39.999
"All right, Kellyanne,
you talk to reporters,

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.934
Stephen, you're from charge
of immigration policy,

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:45.137
and, Donald, you get to be the
conductor of the Trump train.

00:01:45.137 --> 00:01:49.641
Here's your official hat!"

00:01:49.641 --> 00:01:52.679
Now, no one should assume

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.147
that Trump is going to be
easy to beat.

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:56.482
But as his re-Election campaign
ramps up,

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:58.317
he's preparing for
the political fallout

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:01.020
from special counsel
Robert Mueller's looming report

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.788
which could come out
any week now.

00:02:02.788 --> 00:02:04.824
Yesterday, Trump was asked
if he would be in favor

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.558
of making Mueller's
report public,

00:02:06.558 --> 00:02:08.127
and he insisted
that he would be,

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:10.296
although if you listen to
Trump's rambling answers,

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.331
it's hard to believe
that he genuinely wants

00:02:12.331 --> 00:02:13.566
the report to come out.

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.735
-I just won an election

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:19.839
with 63 million votes or so --
63 million.

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:25.044
I got 306 electoral votes
against 223.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.712
That's a tremendous victory.

00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:28.781
And now somebody
just writes a report?

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.116
I think it's ridiculous.

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:32.218
I know that he's conflicted,

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:36.989
and I know that his best friend
is Comey, who's a bad cop.

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:40.526
I know that he put
13 highly conflicted

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:43.762
and, you know, very angry --
I call them angry Democrats in.

00:02:43.762 --> 00:02:46.599
There's no collusion.
There was no collusion.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:49.002
There was no obstruction.
There was no nothing.

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:50.336
With all of that being said,

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.171
I look forward to seeing
the report.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:53.706
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.576
-"With all that being said,"
doesn't really work

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:59.612
when you just said all that.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.280
It's like if a cop
pulled you over and asked

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:02.748
if you'd been drinking,
you said,

00:03:02.748 --> 00:03:04.851
"Well, officer, I had three
beers, three shots of whiskeys,

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:07.253
a screwdriver, a margarita,
two mai tais, a Martini,

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.422
a bottle of wine, six jello
shots, and a line of coke.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:11.257
With all that being said,
I think I'm good to drive.

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.258
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.258 --> 00:03:15.194
But it's important to remember
that Mueller's report

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:16.629
is not the be-all-end-all,

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:18.431
and Russian collusion
is not the only crime

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:19.699
Trump is being investigated for.

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:22.134
In fact, there are multiple
law enforcement agencies

00:03:22.134 --> 00:03:24.470
investigating virtually
every aspect of Trump's life

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.939
from his personal finances
to his business.

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:29.208
And this week, we got
some blockbuster reporting

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:31.410
suggesting that Trump
may have lied to a bank

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.179
about his net worth
to get a loan.

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:35.415
-"The New York Times"
is reporting that years ago,

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:38.050
Deutsche Bank loaned
over $2 billion

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:40.720
to President Trump,
even though they allegedly knew

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:43.155
that he was lying about
his net worth.

00:03:43.155 --> 00:03:46.125
-The story says, "Mr. Trump
told Deutsche Bank

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:47.893
his net worth was about
$3 billion.

00:03:47.893 --> 00:03:50.396
But when the bank employees
reviewed his finances,

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:53.031
they concluded he was worth
about $788 million.

00:03:53.031 --> 00:03:56.802
-He inflated his net worth
by more than $2 billion.

00:03:56.802 --> 00:03:58.671
It's like when you see a guy
on tinder who says

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:00.072
he speaks six languages,

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:01.874
and then he takes you
to Starbucks and goes,

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:03.743
"Can I have a Farpakieno?"

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:04.877
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:08.881
You want a farpakieno?
Make it deuce-o."

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.583
But the craziest
part of this story

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:11.884
is that despite
all the red flags,

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:14.453
Deutsche Bank gave Trump
billions of dollars anyway.

00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:16.122
Time after time,
the bank handed over money,

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:17.590
a total well over $2 billion

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:20.392
to a man who nearly all other
banks had deemed untouchable.

00:04:20.392 --> 00:04:22.294
Aside from his history
of defaults,

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:24.296
he was an attractive borrower.

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:26.366
That's an insane sentence --
A history of defaults

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:28.835
is what makes you
an unattractive borrower.

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.936
It's like an episode
of "dateline" that starts

00:04:30.936 --> 00:04:32.705
"he was an attractive husband,

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:36.042
aside from his history
of murder."

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:39.712
[ Ominous music plays ]

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:42.114
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.114 --> 00:04:44.349
The story is such
a perfect microcosm

00:04:44.349 --> 00:04:46.452
of how the game is rigged
for people like Donald Trump.

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:48.321
The guy allegedly lied
about his net worth

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:49.622
and defaulted on loans,

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:52.525
yet a major bank was happy
to give him $2 billion.

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:54.794
Compare that to
the 2008 financial crisis,

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:56.662
when conservatives were furious
at the idea

00:04:56.662 --> 00:04:58.063
that President Obama
was going to help out

00:04:58.063 --> 00:05:00.733
struggling homeowners who
couldn't pay their mortgages.

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.735
Conservatives said at the time
that if you took out a mortgage

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.737
you couldn't afford,
it was your fault.

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:06.939
You might even remember
this famous rant on CNBC

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.274
by a guy named Rick Santelli.

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:10.509
This is the rant that is
credited by many people

00:05:10.509 --> 00:05:12.145
with starting the Tea Party
movement.

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:15.114
-The government is promoting
bad behavior.

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:17.716
How about this, President
and new administration --

00:05:17.716 --> 00:05:19.351
Why don't you put up a website

00:05:19.351 --> 00:05:22.321
to have people vote
on the Internet as a referendum

00:05:22.321 --> 00:05:25.958
to see if we really want to
subsidize the losers' mortgages.

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:27.092
This is America!

00:05:27.092 --> 00:05:28.594
How many of you people
want to pay

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:31.530
for your neighbors' mortgage
that has an extra bathroom

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:33.999
and can't pay their bills?
Raise their hand.

00:05:33.999 --> 00:05:35.768
How about we all --
[ Audience booing ]

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:38.971
Agh! President Obama,
are you listening?

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:41.340
-To answer your question,
No, he wasn't,

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:42.975
because we used to
have a president

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:46.278
who didn't spend all day
watching cable TV.

00:05:46.278 --> 00:05:50.249
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:52.251
Now if you go on TV and say,

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:53.753
"President Trump,
are you listening?"

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:56.288
He would call in
five minutes later.

00:05:56.288 --> 00:05:58.791
[ As Trump ]
Heard you loud and clear.

00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:00.793
And yet, despite the culture
of criminality and corruption

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:01.927
surrounding the president,

00:06:01.927 --> 00:06:03.095
Republicans are already
falling in line

00:06:03.095 --> 00:06:04.329
with his re-election bid,

00:06:04.329 --> 00:06:06.198
even ones to expressed
reservations about him.

00:06:06.198 --> 00:06:08.834
Take, for example,
Texas Congressman Will Hurd,

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:10.837
who has criticized Trump's
demand for a border wall.

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:12.337
Hurd has cast himself
as a champion

00:06:12.337 --> 00:06:13.605
of bipartisan compromise.

00:06:13.605 --> 00:06:15.975
In fact, in 2017,
he famously went on

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:18.444
a 36-hour road trip
with Democrat Beto O'Rourke.

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:20.646
They even live streamed
parts of it on Facebook.

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:23.549
-After 36 hours and 1,600 miles

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:27.153
from San Antonio
to Washington in a Chevy Impala,

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:30.623
Democrat Beto O'Rourke
and Republican Will Hurd

00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:32.557
have become a little closer.

00:06:32.557 --> 00:06:34.627
-♪ We're the best of friends ♪

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:38.664
on the road, they found a mutual
appreciation for country music,

00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:40.299
fast food --

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:42.768
-Whataburger unites us all.

00:06:42.768 --> 00:06:46.071
-And topics that you'll never
find in any buddy movie.

00:06:46.071 --> 00:06:49.274
-We need to be bringing more
people on the healthcare rolls,

00:06:49.274 --> 00:06:50.409
not fewer.

00:06:50.409 --> 00:06:52.411
-Building a wall from
sea to shining sea

00:06:52.411 --> 00:06:54.279
is the most expensive
and least effective way

00:06:54.279 --> 00:06:55.614
to do border security.

00:06:55.614 --> 00:06:58.117
-Wow, that is the most
policy heavy road trip

00:06:58.117 --> 00:07:00.319
since that documentary
about legalizing weed

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:02.188
starring Cheech &amp; Chong.

00:07:02.188 --> 00:07:02.954
[ Laughter ]

00:07:02.954 --> 00:07:04.356
The road trip went viral,

00:07:04.356 --> 00:07:06.959
and Beto even declined to help
Hurd's Democratic opponent

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:08.894
in 2018 as a sign
of their friendship,

00:07:08.894 --> 00:07:11.196
so naturally, when Hurd
was asked earlier this month

00:07:11.196 --> 00:07:13.999
if he would vote for his friend,
Beto, over the president,

00:07:13.999 --> 00:07:15.634
he was repeatedly criticized.

00:07:15.634 --> 00:07:18.371
Hurd said he would definitely
vote for Donald Trump.

00:07:18.371 --> 00:07:21.307
-Who would you vote for between
Beto O'Rourke and Donald Trump?

00:07:21.307 --> 00:07:24.409
-My plan is to vote for
the Republican nominee.

00:07:24.409 --> 00:07:26.612
-Man, you know it's bad
when you can't even say the name

00:07:26.612 --> 00:07:28.414
of the guy you're voting for.

00:07:28.414 --> 00:07:30.716
Republicans are gonna have to
print out lawn signs

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:33.519
that say "Republican nominee,
whoever that is, 2020."

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:34.386
[ Laughter ]

00:07:34.386 --> 00:07:36.155
Also, you're going to toss Beto

00:07:36.155 --> 00:07:37.523
after all you've been through?

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:39.858
Because if you went on
a road trip and ate Whataburger,

00:07:39.858 --> 00:07:42.662
I can only imagine fart cloud
you two shared.

00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:44.029
[ Laughter ]

00:07:44.029 --> 00:07:45.864
Right-wing pundits who
distanced themselves from Trump

00:07:45.864 --> 00:07:46.966
are falling in line, too,

00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:48.634
like former Fox News host,
Glenn Beck.

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:50.369
Beck spent most of his years

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:52.405
as one of the most unhinged
voices on Fox,

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:54.707
warning that nefarious forces
were destroying the country,

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:56.742
and trying to prove
that Obama was a dictator

00:07:56.742 --> 00:07:58.677
by circling random letters
on a chalkboard

00:07:58.677 --> 00:08:01.080
like he was playing a dickhead
version of the Jumble.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:04.817
-Obama, the left,
internationalists,

00:08:04.817 --> 00:08:07.953
graft,
ACORN-style organizations,

00:08:07.953 --> 00:08:11.157
revolution,
and hidden agenda.

00:08:11.157 --> 00:08:13.158
O...L...I...

00:08:13.158 --> 00:08:16.595
G...A...R...H.

00:08:16.595 --> 00:08:17.562
[ Laughter ]

00:08:17.562 --> 00:08:18.998
One letter is missing.

00:08:18.998 --> 00:08:21.934
And then tie them all together
into one word.

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:24.236
Oligarch.

00:08:24.236 --> 00:08:26.004
The one that's missing...

00:08:26.004 --> 00:08:28.307
is "Y."
-No.

00:08:28.307 --> 00:08:31.544
No. That's not -- That's not
the letter you're missing.

00:08:31.544 --> 00:08:33.846
You spelled oligarchy without
a "C."

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:35.982
That's oligarhy.

00:08:35.982 --> 00:08:38.250
You're closer to spelling
Olive Garden.

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:39.919
[ Laughter ]

00:08:39.919 --> 00:08:41.387
Now, now...

00:08:41.387 --> 00:08:44.456
[ Applause ]

00:08:44.456 --> 00:08:47.493
In 2016, Beck seemed to have
a change of heart.

00:08:47.493 --> 00:08:49.562
HE apologized for extremist
rhetoric,

00:08:49.562 --> 00:08:50.997
said he would not vote
for Trump,

00:08:50.997 --> 00:08:52.264
and even told
"The New York Times,"

00:08:52.264 --> 00:08:54.233
"I think he could be one
of the most dangerous presidents

00:08:54.233 --> 00:08:55.635
to ever come into
the oval office."

00:08:55.635 --> 00:08:57.102
At the time, many suspected

00:08:57.102 --> 00:08:59.071
this was all just an act
to rebrand himself,

00:08:59.071 --> 00:09:02.008
and when he went on Fox News
this week to talk about 2020,

00:09:02.008 --> 00:09:03.342
he finally dropped the act.

00:09:03.342 --> 00:09:07.412
-I will tell you this --
if the Republicans don't win

00:09:07.412 --> 00:09:08.813
in this next election,

00:09:08.813 --> 00:09:10.783
I think we are officially

00:09:10.783 --> 00:09:13.185
at the end of the country
as we know it.

00:09:13.185 --> 00:09:15.754
-Oh, my God. Hold on, you guys.

00:09:15.754 --> 00:09:18.224
He's on Fox News...

00:09:18.224 --> 00:09:19.625
[ Laughter ]

00:09:19.625 --> 00:09:23.161
...talking about the end
of the United States...

00:09:23.161 --> 00:09:26.599
which can mean only one thing --
"F.U."

00:09:26.599 --> 00:09:27.766
[ Laughter ]

00:09:27.766 --> 00:09:29.768
And I'm sorry, but we're not --

00:09:29.768 --> 00:09:31.937
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:31.937 --> 00:09:35.074
We're not taking
political advice --

00:09:35.074 --> 00:09:36.942
Nobody wants to take
political advice

00:09:36.942 --> 00:09:39.645
from divorced Santa Claus
over here.

00:09:39.645 --> 00:09:41.413
And we can tell he's pandering
to Trump

00:09:41.413 --> 00:09:43.616
because he's started to
dress like The Colonel.

00:09:43.616 --> 00:09:45.084
[ Laughter ]

00:09:45.084 --> 00:09:47.085
Republicans are falling in line
with Trump's re-election bid

00:09:47.085 --> 00:09:48.587
despite the culture
of corruption

00:09:48.587 --> 00:09:49.921
and criminality around him.

00:09:49.921 --> 00:09:52.257
So many of his closest
associates have been indicted,

00:09:52.257 --> 00:09:55.027
and every aspect of his personal
life is being investigated.

00:09:55.027 --> 00:09:57.396
At this point,
in order not to find a crime,

00:09:57.396 --> 00:09:59.097
you'd have to be a --
-Bad cop.

00:09:59.097 --> 00:10:00.833
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:00.833 --> 00:10:02.201
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:02.201 --> 00:10:04.403 line:0%
♪♪

